{"resourceIdentifier":"3738","resourceName":"Triunfo do Xingu Grouped REDD+ Project","description":"The Triunfo do Xingu Grouped REDD+ Project (hereinafter also referred to as “TdX”) is composed by seven rural properties located in the Municipality of Altamira, in the south region of the State of Pará. According to the geo-referencing data, the total area of the project is established at 10,636.02 ha. This project aims to be registered under the Verified Carbon Standard (VCS) to avoid unplanned deforestation (AUD), combating the decreased carbon stock in the Brazilian Legal Amazon. \r\nThe crediting period of the project is 30 years. The start date is on August 31, 2022 and, therefore, the crediting period is expected to end on August 30, 2052. The baseline scenario developed is going to be used for the first six years of the project, since, according to VCS requirements, these six years are the maximum period until a baseline scenario reassessment needs to be done. The present analysis, that will be employed in the project validation and future project verifications, is going to be done in a conservative approach, keeping the project consistent.\r\nThe TdX aims for the following objectives: environmental benefits through a successful monitoring system; economic benefits resulting in regional development through investments in local communities. To execute the installation of this project and to achieve its objectives the VCU generation is very important. A baseline reduction of 1,565,285.35 tCO2e of GHG is expected over six years, associated with the avoided deforestation of 6,167.07 ha.","location":{"latitude":-5.619138,"longitude":-53.687711},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2025-10-02","endExclusive":"2025-11-02","endInclusive":"2025-11-01"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3738"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Pará"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"pro